# Nagmon (נגמון) - the game

A private, family learning game in Hebrew: maths, geometry, English, science
and logic inside a monster-collecting adventure. Each child has a profile;
there is a parents' area. This repo is **private** and is **not a fork**: the
code of the game, built on data from [Tuxemon](https://github.com/Tuxemon/Tuxemon)
(GPL-3.0, with CC-BY-SA art, see `LICENSE` and `ATTRIBUTIONS.md`).

Family details, device logs and field data are **not** here. They live in the
private data repo `YuvalNag/nagmon-data`.

## What is in the repo

| Folder | What |
|---|---|
| `app/` | The app: React + Phaser + Capacitor (Android). `app/public/game` is the generated game data. |
| `tools/app/` | The data build: turns `mods/` into `app/public/game`. |
| `mods/nagmon`, `mods/tuxemon` | The game data the build reads (monsters, maps, texts, sounds, art). |
| `tuxemon/`, `nagmon/` | Python packages the data build imports. |
| `tests/app/` | Python tests of the data build and of the content. |
| `docs/app/`, `docs/kids/` | Specs (SDD), status and plans. |
| `.github/workflows/` | `app.yml` (checks, browser, APK, emulator), `data.yml` (data build and Python tests). |

## Build and test

Needs Node 22 and Python 3.12+.

```bash
# the app
cd app
npm ci
npm run typecheck      # tsc --noEmit
npm test               # vitest
npm run build          # tsc + vite build
npm run e2e            # Playwright, after: npx playwright install chromium

# the data (from the repo root)
python -m venv .venv && . .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt pytest numpy scipy
python -m tools.app.build_data --check   # app/public/game is up to date with mods/
python -m tools.app.build_data           # regenerate it
pytest tests/app -q
```

`app/public/game` is committed. After a change in `mods/` or `tools/app/`, run
the data build and commit the result; CI fails when they differ.

## Art

The raw art sources (`art_sources/`, 48 MB, except the Solar monsters the
build reads), the intro frames and the unused Tuxemon music and fonts are **not** in this repo. They go to the
private art repo `YuvalNag/nagmon-art` (see `docs/app/ART_DELIVERY.md`).

